* {{sense|broadcasting}} In North American English, a year-long group of episodes of a television or radio show is called a {{m|en|season|id=Q3464665}}, whereas the word {{m|en|series}} is a synonym of {{m|en|program}} or {{m|en|show}}.
* {{sense|mathematics}} Beginning students often confuse {{m|en||series}} with {{m|en|sequence}}.

